A stop goes through a Thread capability without RIGHT_W,
so a capability that only lends a thread time stops it:
a call goes through only a capability with the rights its operation needs.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call went through a capability without the rights its operation needs

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -913,7 +913,7 @@ static int dispatch(struct thread *t, uint32_t op, uint32_t slot, uint32_t *arg)
         err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_process(t, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         break;
     case CAP_THREAD:
-        err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) ? op_thread(t, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
+        err = (cap.rights & RIGHT_W) || op == OP_THREAD_STOP ? op_thread(t, &cap, op, arg) : KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
         break;
     case CAP_NOTIFICATION:
         err = op_notification(t, slot, &cap, op, arg);
